     exp:"Your brokerage account has NO tax advantages, but also NO restrictions on when you can pull money out. This is where we put investments you plan to sell by May 2027. We picked energy plays (XLE, XOP) and KTOS here because energy prices are elevated due to geopolitical tensions, making these good near-term trades. You'll owe capital gains tax when you sell — if you hold over 1 year, you get the lower long-term capital gains rate (15%).",
     rules:["Gains taxed as capital gains (15-20% if held >1 year)","No contribution limits","Can withdraw anytime","Best for: positions you plan to sell within 1-2 years"]},
    {name:"Roth IRA",icon:"🌱",color:"var(--green)",strat:"LONG-TERM GROWTH (Tax-free forever)",
     exp:"Your Roth IRA is the most powerful investment account you have. Money grows TAX-FREE and withdrawals in retirement are TAX-FREE. That's why we put the highest-growth picks here (ITA, UFO, HII, PLTR) — every dollar of growth will never be taxed. At 35, you have 25+ years of tax-free compounding ahead of you. The $150B+ defense spending wave will play out over 4-5 years, and these positions will compound those gains tax-free.",
     rules:["All growth is TAX-FREE forever","2026 contribution limit: $7,000/year","Can withdraw contributions anytime (not gains until 59½)","Best for: highest-growth positions"]},
    {name:"IRA",icon:"🏦",color:"var(--blue)",strat:"LONG-TERM STEADY (Tax-deferred growth)",
     exp:"Your Traditional IRA gives you a tax deduction NOW and taxes you when you withdraw in retirement. We put steadier, dividend-paying positions here (CIBR, FENY, LMT) because dividends reinvested in an IRA aren't taxed annually — they compound without a tax drag. Lockheed's $13.60/year dividend per share grows untaxed here. Think of this as your 'slow and steady wins the race' account.",
     rules:["Contributions may be tax-deductible","Growth is tax-deferred","Taxed as ordinary income on withdrawal","Best for: dividend stocks and steady compounders"]}
